nvestee items embedded in the profit-before-tax bridge that this schema captures in aggregate but not line-by-line. On trailing earnings, P/E of 61.9x looks expensive, though that multiple is mechanically inflated by the depressed FY2025 PAT rather than necessarily reflecting genuine overvaluation; P/B of 0.84x is below book. The business itself -- diversified, market-leading across multiple sectors including leisure (a direct tourism-recovery play) -- looks structurally strong even though the FY2025 numbers were weak (Annual Report FY2025, p.301-303).", "gaps_note": "Macro & Industry Outlook (10% weight) unavailable -- no CBSL/IMF/World Bank/news data source exists in this project; the remaining five pillars are renormalized to sum to 100% (Financial Quality 33.3%, Growth 22.2%, Valuation 22.2%, Business Quality 16.7%, Governance & Risk 5.6%). Governance & Risk is also necessarily thin -- no circulars/disclosures feed exists (deliberately disabled this session), so insider transactions, board changes, and rights issues cannot be verified directly; the score below reflects only what's visible in audited financial statements and public market data.", "source_financials_asof": null, "source_market_data_asof": "2026-07-14", "pillar_scores": {"financial_quality": {"score": 4.0, "weight_used": 0.3333333333333333, "rationale": "FY2025 Group ROE just 1.65%, ROA 0.82%, net margin 2.2% -- weak by any standard, and PAT fell 42.9% YoY (12.13bn to 6.92bn), the sharpest earnings decline of any pilot company. Current ratio 1.23x, debt/equity 0.43x are unremarkable. The PBT bridge includes volatile insurance-contract-liability changes, investment-property fair value changes, and equity-accounted investee results, which this schema captures in the PBT bottom line but not as separate line items.", "citations": ["manual_9bf2d12ecda48b2a p.303 (balance sheet)"]}, "growth_outlook": {"score": 5.5, "weight_used": 0.22222222222222224, "rationale": "Revenue grew 13.2% YoY (280.8bn to 317.4bn) even as profit fell sharply -- a genuine growth/profitability divergence (margin compression), not a top-line problem. JKH's leisure segment gives it direct exposure to Sri Lankan tourism recovery, a plausible multi-year tailwind this project cannot independently forecast.", "citations": ["manual_9bf2d12ecda48b2a p.301 (income statement)"]}, "valuation": {"score": 4.0, "weight_used": 0.22222222222222224, "rationale": "P/E of 61.9x is very expensive on trailing earnings, but this is mechanically inflated by the depressed FY2025 PAT just described -- a normalized-earnings P/E would look materially lower, though this project has not built a normalized-earnings estimate. P/B of 0.84x (below book) is a genuinely cheap signal on assets. No dividend data on file for JKH -- yield/payout are gaps, not zeros.", "citations": ["market_data as of 2026-07-14"]}, "business_quality": {"score": 7.5, "weight_used": 0.16666666666666666, "rationale": "Sri Lanka's largest, most diversified listed conglomerate -- leadership positions across transportation/ports, consumer foods, retail, leisure, property, and financial services provide real diversification and multiple growth vectors. This structural strength is why the score is materially higher than the Financial Quality and Valuation pillars despite the weak FY2025 earnings year.", "citations": ["manual_9bf2d12ecda48b2a p.301"]}, "macro_industry": {"score": null, "weight_used": null, "rationale": "", "citations": []}, "governance_risk": {"score": 7.0, "weight_used": 0.05555555555555556, "rationale": "Widely regarded as one of the best-governed companies on the CSE given its scale and long operating history, but this project has no disclosures/circulars feed to verify recent board or ownership changes directly -- the score reflects general blue-chip standing, tempered by that verification gap.", "citations": ["manual_9bf2d12ecda48b2a p.303"]}}, "weights_used": {"financial_quality": 0.3333333333333333, "growth_outlook": 0.22222222222222224, "valuation": 0.22222222222222224, "business_quality": 0.16666666666666666, "governance_risk": 0.05555555555555556}, "key_reasons": ["Most diversified blue-chip franchise on the CSE, with leadership positions across six distinct business segments", "Revenue still grew 13.2% YoY despite the profit decline -- the weakness is margin/one-off-item driven, not a demand problem", "P/B of 0.84x is below book value, and the depressed FY2025 earnings likely understate normalized earning power"], "watch_factors": ["PAT fell 42.9% YoY -- the single largest earnings decline in this pilot set; whether this reverses in FY2026 is the central open question", "No dividend data on file for JKH in this database -- a real gap, not confirmed nil", "PBT is affected by insurance-contract-liability changes and equity-accounted-investee results that this schema doesn't itemize separately -- a deeper read of the segment notes would sharpen this further"], "horizon_notes": {"6m": "FY2026 Q1 interim results (once available) will show whether the FY2025 profit decline was a one-off or the start of a trend.", "1y": "If PAT reverts toward the FY2024 level (12.1bn), the current 61.9x trailing P/E would look dramatically cheaper in hindsight.", "3y": "Leisure-segment exposure gives JKH a genuine multi-year tourism-recovery lever this project cannot independently forecast (no macro/tourism data source).", "5y": "Diversification across six segments is JKH's core long-run advantage, but this project has not built segment-level financial tracking to test it directly."}}, "ratios": {"COMPANY": [{"period_label": "FY2024 (year ended 31 March 2024)", "period_end_date": "2024-03-31", "gross_profit": 1133495.0, "gross_margin": 0.3886637246733119, "operating_margin": 3.580391168533701, "ebitda": 10441817.0, "ebitda_margin": 3.580391168533701, "net_margin": 1.4580741944664466, "roe": 0.020608239400255978, "roa": 0.013869838065479532, "roce": 0.03798897261428764, "current_ratio": 1.9941125657010905, "quic